==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|wunta}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*wundō||a wound}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*wundaz||wounded}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*wan-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*awa(n)-}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|Wunn}}, Dutch {{m|nl|wond}}, English {{m|en|wound}}, Icelandic {{m|is|und}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvʊn.də/|lang=de}}
